# Extracting Text from a Document with JavaScript

Here's a robust function that handles the most common document types in the browser: plain text, HTML, PDF, DOCX, and images (via OCR is out of scope, but noted).

## Approach

The right method depends on the **file type** and the **source** (a `File`, a URL, or a DOM node). I'll give you one entry-point function that dispatches based on MIME type, plus the per-type extractors.

## Code

```javascript
/**
 * Extract plain text from a document.
 * @param {File|string} source - A File object, or a URL to fetch.
 * @param {Object} [opts]
 * @param {string} [opts.type]  - Override MIME type detection.
 * @returns {Promise<string>}
 */
async function extractText(source, opts = {}) {
  // 1. Normalize to { blob, mime } ==============================
  let blob, mime;

  if (source instanceof File || source instanceof Blob) {
    blob = source;
    mime = opts.type || source.type || "";
  } else if (typeof source === "string") {
    const res = await fetch(source);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Fetch failed: ${res.status}`);
    blob = await res.blob();
    mime = opts.type || res.headers.get("content-type") || "";
  } else {
