# JavaScript Text Extraction Function

Here's a comprehensive function to extract text from an HTML document, with options for customization:

```javascript
/**
 * Extracts visible text content from a document or DOM element.
 * @param {Document|Element} node - The document or element to extract text from.
 * @param {Object} [options] - Configuration options.
 * @param {string[]} [options.excludeTags] - Tags to skip entirely (e.g. script, style).
 * @param {boolean} [options.preserveWhitespace] - If true, keeps raw whitespace.
 * @param {boolean} [options.includeHidden] - If true, includes elements hidden via CSS.
 * @returns {string} Extracted, cleaned text.
 */
function extractText(node = document, options = {}) {
  const {
    excludeTags = ['script', 'style', 'noscript', 'template', 'svg'],
    preserveWhitespace = false,
    includeHidden = false
  } = options;

  const excludeSet = new Set(excludeTags.map(t => t.toUpperCase()));
  const root = node.body || node; // use <body> if a full document is passed
  let result = '';

  function isVisible(el) {
    if (includeHidden) return true;
    if (!(el instanceof Element)) return true;
    const style = window.getComputedStyle(el);
    return style.display !== 'none' &&
           style.visibility !== 'hidden' &&
           el.getAttribute('aria-hidden') !== 'true';
  }

  function walk(current) {
    if (current.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {
      result += current.textContent;
      return;
    }

    if (current.nodeType !== Node.ELEMENT_NODE) return;

    if (excludeSet.has(current.tagName)) return;
    if (!isVisible(current)) return;

    for (const child of current.childNodes) {
      walk(child);
    }

    // Add line breaks after block-level elements for readability
    const blockTags = new Set([
      'P', 'DIV', 'BR', 'LI', 'TR', 'H1', 'H2', 'H3',
      'H4', 'H5', 'H6', 'SECTION', 'ARTICLE', 'HEADER', 'FOOTER'
    ]);
    if (blockTags.has(current.tagName)) {
      result += '\n';
    }
  }

  walk(root);

  if (!preserveWhitespace) {
    result = result
      .replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' ')       // collapse spaces/tabs
      .replace(/\n\s*\n+/g, '\n')    // collapse multiple blank lines
      .split('\n')
      .map(line => line.trim())
      .filter(line => line.length > 0)
      .join('\n');
  }

  return result.trim();
}
```

## Usage examples

```javascript
// Extract all visible text from the current page
const pageText = extractText(document);
console.log(pageText);

// Extract text from a specific element
const section = document.querySelector('#article');
const sectionText = extractText(section);

// Preserve raw whitespace (no cleanup)
const rawText = extractText(document, { preserveWhitespace: true });

// Include hidden elements too
const allText = extractText(document, { includeHidden: true });

// Exclude additional tags (e.g. navigation, ads)
const mainText = extractText(document, {
  excludeTags: ['script', 'style', 'nav', 'footer', 'aside']
});
```

## Key features

- **Skips non-content tags** (`script`, `style`, etc.) by default, configurable via `excludeTags`.
- **Respects CSS visibility** — ignores `display: none` and `visibility: hidden` elements unless `includeHidden` is set.
- **Adds line breaks** after block-level elements for more readable output.
- **Normalizes whitespace** (collapses repeated spaces/newlines, trims lines) unless `preserveWhitespace` is `true`.
- Works on the full `document` or any specific DOM element/subtree.

## Note for non-browser environments

This function relies on `window`, `document`, and DOM APIs, so it works in browsers. For **Node.js**, you'd need a DOM implementation like `jsdom`:

```javascript
const { JSDOM } = require('jsdom');
const dom = new JSDOM(htmlString);
global.window = dom.window;
global.document = dom.window.document;
global.Node = dom.window.Node;
global.Element = dom.window.Element;

const text = extractText(document);
```

Let me know if you need a version tailored to Node.js (e.g., using `jsdom` or `cheerio`), or one for extracting text from PDFs/other file types instead of HTML.

